			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846008">
									

<blockquote>
<p>This was created by an &quot;anartist&quot; who is all about practical stuff. Would probably involve exploration of Whiteboard Dimension to her old notes and such.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, tell me about this: what do her old notes say? Why are they of interest now? What's in the whiteboard dimension that makes it interesting to explore?</p>
<p>I think my concern with this idea is that it's what I'd term 'overbroad': it's the kinda idea that opens you up to all kinds of cool and interesting things you could do with it, which in turn means finding the one that's actually interesting is really hard.</p>
<p>I like the idea of tying an anartist in here; and like, exploring what she got up to using this and stuff, but my largest concern is really just that I don't have a good idea of where this goes or anything. The actual whiteboard might be a touch overcomplex in how it works: it feels like it could be streamlined to have more focus with a few less anomalous bits to it but I don't think this is necessarily a huge issue as long as you do something interesting with it.</p>

